      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Materials"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "150 m DK cotton in colour A (main). 150 m DK cotton in colour B (contrast). Two 100 m balls of each colour, with some left over from each."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "18 htr × 14 rows = 10 × 10 cm in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook, lightly blocked."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Half treble (htr). UK term; US equivalent is half double crochet (hdc)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "With colour A, ch 57. (The foundation chain sets the width, 54 ch for the htr stitches, plus 3 turning chain. Each htr occupies approximately 0.55 cm at this gauge; 54 htr = approx. 30 cm.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Row 1 (colour A): ch 3 (t-ch, counts as htr), htr in 3rd ch from hook, htr in each ch across (54 htr). Turn."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Row 2 (colour A): ch 2 (t-ch, does NOT count as a stitch. Work first htr into the base of this ch 2), htr in each st to end, htr into top of t-ch from row 1 (54 htr). On the final yarn-over of the last htr, pull through with colour B. Drop colour A at the side. Turn."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rows 3, 4 (colour B): same as rows 1, 2. Change to colour A on final yarn-over of row 4."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Continue alternating 2 rows colour A / 2 rows colour B until the runner measures 90 cm from the foundation chain (approx. 90 rows total, 45 stripe pairs). Fasten off both colours."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "tip"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Carry the yarn not in use up the side edge rather than cutting it at every stripe change. Loop the carried yarn loosely around the working yarn at the turn so it doesn't pull the edge in. This halves the number of ends to weave in."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in all ends along the side edges. Light wet-blocking lays the runner flat and sharpens the stripe edges. Pin to size and leave until dry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine-wash on 30°C gentle cycle. Lay flat to dry. The cotton softens with each wash."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
